Make SDCC's recursive tree decomposition walks iterative.

In a browser, every WebAssembly call runs on the worker's native stack,
which is limited to a few hundred KB (Safari reported "Maximum call stack
size exceeded"). This patch turns the recursive walks of the register
allocator and of the lospre and naddr optimizations into loops with an
explicit stack. The generated code is unchanged; compiling GB Studio's
engine then fits in 100 KB of stack (measured with node --stack-size).

Applies with `patch -p0` on top of SDCC r15267 and the GBDK-2020 patches.

